# =============================================================================
# Equal-grain pair at -20 C starting from TANGENT CONTACT, quarter of the
# cross-section: one grain, mirror plane at x = 0, axis at y = 0. Pair with
# experiment/molaro/molaro_T-20_hsat_150h_a1e-3_dirichlet_mirror.opts
# (batch: studies/molaro_2019/batches/demmenie_tangent_T-20.txt).
#
# WHY. The first saturated run (..._R84um_r14um_mirror, 2026-10-06) started
# from a neck already 28 um wide. Its fitted exponent (0.21) depends on how
# long that neck "had been growing": a free fit takes 4.8 h, the
# Gibbs-Thomson prediction says 16 h, and with 16 h the same data give 0.28
# (studies/molaro_2019/demmenie/README.md). Starting from grains that just
# touch gives the clock a physical zero. Everything else is IDENTICAL to that
# run: grain radius, eps, mesh spacing, air padding, wall distance.
#
# GEOMETRY. R = 84.4 um, centre at x = R, so the sharp sphere touches the
# mirror plane x = 0 at one point; its image is the second grain. With
# -ic_grain_union the phi = 0.5 contour is the sharp surface.
#
# RESOLUTION. eps = 1.18e-7 m. Neck floor sqrt(12 eps R) = 10.93 um radius,
# i.e. 21.9 um WIDTH: below that the neck is set by the diffuse band, not by
# physics, and those samples are NOT to be fitted. The Gibbs-Thomson
# prediction reaches that width after about 3 h and 33.5 um (the first fitted
# width of the earlier run) after about 16 h.
#
# DOMAIN. Lx = 2R + 52.7 um of air beyond the far cap = 221.53 um at the
# same h = eps/sqrt(2); Ly = 188 um as before.
#
# Measure: bash postprocess/run_batch_measure.sh <run_dir>   (passes --mirror-x0)
# =============================================================================

-axisym 1
-ic_grain_union 1
-ic_type multi_grains
-dim 2
-Lx 2.21529e-04
-Ly 1.88000e-04
-Lz 0

-ice_grain_cx 8.44000e-05               # = R: tangent to the mirror plane x = 0
-ice_grain_cy 0.0
-ice_grain_R  8.44e-5
-ice_grain_ax 8.44e-5
-ice_grain_ay 8.44e-5

-Nx 2655                                # h = eps/sqrt(2) = 8.3439e-08
-Ny 2254                                # 5.99M nodes, 18.0M DoF
-Nz 1
-eps 1.1800e-07
-eps_valid_temp -20

-delt_t 1.0e-4
-periodic 0
